  {
    id: 'ef2',
    title: '接力赛的信',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 9,
    lines: [
      { no: 1, text: 'Dear Sam, Thank you for your letter of last month. I am writing to tell you about sports meeting' },
      { no: 2, text: 'that was held at our school last week. I take part in the four by one hundred relay,' },
      { no: 3, text: 'which is the most excited event of the whole meeting and the one everybody loves.' },
      { no: 4, text: 'Our team practised hardly four times a week, and sometimes we stayed until dark.' },
      { no: 5, text: 'At the beginning we kept to drop the baton, so we spent two weeks only practising the pass.' },
      { no: 6, text: 'Our teacher stopped us and said that timing are far more important than speed in such a race.' },
      { no: 7, text: 'Then he made us to pass the baton slowly again and again until everyone knew the right moment.' },
      { no: 8, text: 'On the final day it was rained, so the track was wet and everyone had to be careful.' },
      { no: 9, text: 'Two runner fell over in the first leg, and our team lost the chance to win.' },
      { no: 10, text: 'We finished third in the end, and our classmates all praised ourselves for the three months of hard work.' },
    ],
    fixes: [
      { no: 1, type: '增', from: 'about', to: 'a', explain: 'about 后缺不定冠词，a sports meeting 泛指一次运动会。' },
      { no: 2, type: '改', from: 'I take part', to: 'I took part', explain: '叙述上周的运动会，谓语动词用一般过去时。' },
      { no: 3, type: '改', from: 'excited', to: 'exciting', explain: '修饰 event 这类事物用 -ing 形容词，excited 只用于人的感受。' },
      { no: 4, type: '改', from: 'practised hardly', to: 'practised hard', explain: 'hardly 意为“几乎不”，要表达“刻苦训练”用副词 hard。' },
      { no: 5, type: '改', from: 'kept to drop', to: 'kept dropping', explain: 'keep 后接动名词，kept dropping 表示反复掉棒。' },
      { no: 6, type: '改', from: 'timing are', to: 'timing is', explain: 'timing 是不可数名词，从句谓语用单数。' },
      { no: 7, type: '删', from: 'to', to: '删去 to', explain: 'make sb do sth 的宾语补足语是不带 to 的不定式，to 多余。' },
      { no: 8, type: '改', from: 'was rained', to: 'rained', explain: '表示“下雨”时 rain 是不及物动词，没有被动形式。' },
      { no: 9, type: '改', from: 'Two runner', to: 'Two runners', explain: 'two 后接可数名词复数。' },
      { no: 10, type: '改', from: 'praised ourselves', to: 'praised us', explain: '主语 classmates 与宾语“我们”不是同一批人，不能用反身代词。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'ef3',
    title: '社区图书角日记',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 8,
    lines: [
      { no: 1, text: 'Saturday, 12 April. It is warm today, and our community opens a small reading corner near the gate.' },
      { no: 2, text: 'My cousin and I went there after lunch. The idea was a first one put forward by Mrs. Gao.' },
      { no: 3, text: 'Mrs. Gao, what has lived in our street for forty years, talked about such a place for years.' },
      { no: 4, text: 'The corner sit in a glass room, so people can see the shelves and the books from outside.' },
      { no: 5, text: 'The shelves were made of old wood, and a long table stood in the middle with four chair around it.' },
      { no: 6, text: 'There were about six hundreds books, each with a small white card in front.' },
      { no: 7, text: 'Most of them were given by families who had finished read them and had no place to send them.' },
      { no: 8, text: 'A volunteer wrote our names on cards so what we could borrow two books at a time.' },
      { no: 9, text: 'I borrowed two books about old bridges and stayed in the glass room for a full whole hour.' },
      { no: 10, text: 'Before leaving I gave away four of my own books, for I think such corner makes our street warmer.' },
    ],
    fixes: [
      { no: 1, type: '改', from: 'community opens', to: 'community opened', explain: '日记记述当天已经发生完的事，opens 要改一般过去时 opened。' },
      { no: 2, type: '改', from: 'a first one', to: 'the first one', explain: '序数词前用定冠词 the，不用 a。' },
      { no: 3, type: '改', from: 'what', to: 'who', explain: '非限制性定语从句的先行词是人，关系词用 who，what 不能引导定语从句。' },
      { no: 4, type: '改', from: 'corner sit', to: 'corner sits', explain: '主语 the corner 是第三人称单数，谓语加 -s。' },
      { no: 5, type: '改', from: 'four chair', to: 'four chairs', explain: 'four 后接可数名词复数。' },
      { no: 6, type: '改', from: 'six hundreds books', to: 'six hundred books', explain: '具体数字后的 hundred 不加 s，hundreds of 才用复数。' },
      { no: 7, type: '改', from: 'finished read', to: 'finished reading', explain: 'finish 后接动名词作宾语。' },
      { no: 8, type: '改', from: 'so what', to: 'so that', explain: '目的状语从句用 so that 引导，what 不能引导从句。' },
      { no: 9, type: '删', from: 'whole', to: '删去 whole', explain: 'a full hour 已表示“整整一小时”，whole 与 full 重复多余。' },
      { no: 10, type: '增', from: 'such', to: 'a', explain: 'such 修饰单数可数名词时要说 such a corner，句中缺冠词 a。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'ef4',
    title: '给校长的建议信',
    exam: '高考',
    mins: 9,
    lines: [
      { no: 1, text: 'Dear Mr. President, I am Li Ming from Grade 2. Our school library has opened for twenty years.' },
      { no: 2, text: 'Last term many of my classmates went there every week, and some borrowed two or three book each.' },
      { no: 3, text: 'However, there is only one small reading room, and it have twenty seats for three hundred students.' },
      { no: 4, text: 'Some students come here for a quiet place to sit, and others stand by the window for prepare for a test.' },
      { no: 5, text: 'The room is too crowded, but we have to wait outside or sit on the steps.' },
      { no: 6, text: 'The rules of the library are simple, and everybody must follow it before borrowing a book.' },
      { no: 7, text: 'Our librarian explained the rules us kindly on the first school day of this term.' },
      { no: 8, text: 'She said the room was not very much big, but it could be used better.' },
      { no: 9, text: 'We are not allowed to eating anything in the reading room, so nobody drinks water there.' },
      { no: 10, text: 'I hope the school will build a second reading room, for it is pleasure to study in a quiet place.' },
    ],
    fixes: [
      { no: 1, type: '改', from: 'library has opened', to: 'library has been open', explain: 'for twenty years 要与延续性状态连用，open 在此是形容词，has been open。' },
      { no: 2, type: '改', from: 'three book', to: 'three books', explain: 'two or three 后接可数名词复数。' },
      { no: 3, type: '改', from: 'it have', to: 'it has', explain: '主语 it 第三人称单数，have 变 has。' },
      { no: 4, type: '改', from: 'for prepare', to: 'to prepare', explain: '表目的用不定式 to prepare，for 后不能接动词原形。' },
      { no: 5, type: '改', from: 'but', to: 'so', explain: '前后是因果关系“太挤，所以只能等在门外”，用 so 不用 but。' },
      { no: 6, type: '改', from: 'follow it', to: 'follow them', explain: '代词指代复数名词 the rules，要用 them。' },
      { no: 7, type: '增', from: 'rules', to: 'to', explain: 'explain sth to sb 缺介词 to，应为 explained the rules to us。' },
      { no: 8, type: '删', from: 'much', to: '删去 much', explain: 'very big 已足够，very much 不能修饰形容词 big。' },
      { no: 9, type: '改', from: 'to eating', to: 'to eat', explain: 'be allowed to do sth 用不定式，to 后接动词原形。' },
      { no: 10, type: '增', from: 'is', to: 'a', explain: 'pleasure 表“一件乐事”是可数名词，缺冠词 a，it is a pleasure to do。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'ef5',
    title: '第一次英语演讲',
    exam: '中考',
    mins: 8,
    lines: [
      { no: 1, text: 'Last month I gave my first English speech at school. My hands were shake and my face was hot.' },
      { no: 2, text: 'It was a first time for me to stand in front of so many students and teachers.' },
      { no: 3, text: 'I asked my English teacher for advices, and she helped me change my notes again and again.' },
      { no: 4, text: 'Many parents came to the school that day, and everyone look at me when I walked in.' },
      { no: 5, text: 'My notes were short, just enough to help me remembering the three main ideas of my speech.' },
      { no: 6, text: 'Although I was nervous, but I did not stop and I finished the whole speech.' },
      { no: 7, text: 'When I finished, a girl from Class 3 came up and said my speech made I very happy.' },
      { no: 8, text: 'My teacher was pride of me, and she said it in front of the whole class.' },
      { no: 9, text: 'I have learned that giving a speech is not easy thing, but I am not afraid of it now.' },
      { no: 10, text: 'Now I feel much bravely than before, and I will speak again at the end of this term.' },
    ],
    fixes: [
      { no: 1, type: '改', from: 'were shake', to: 'were shaking', explain: '过去进行时是 were 加现在分词，were shake 结构不完整。' },
      { no: 2, type: '改', from: 'a first', to: 'the first', explain: 'It was the first time for sb to do sth，序数词前用 the。' },
      { no: 3, type: '改', from: 'advices', to: 'advice', explain: 'advice 是不可数名词，没有 advices 这种复数形式。' },
      { no: 4, type: '改', from: 'everyone look', to: 'everyone looked', explain: 'that day 是过去时间，谓语用一般过去时。' },
      { no: 5, type: '改', from: 'help me remembering', to: 'help me remember', explain: 'help sb do sth 用不带 to 的不定式作宾补。' },
      { no: 6, type: '删', from: 'but', to: '删去 but', explain: 'although 与 but 不能同时使用，连词重复多余。' },
      { no: 7, type: '改', from: 'made I', to: 'made me', explain: '作 made 的宾语要用宾格 me，不用主格 I。' },
      { no: 8, type: '改', from: 'pride of', to: 'proud of', explain: 'be 后接形容词 proud，be proud of 是固定搭配。' },
      { no: 9, type: '增', from: 'easy', to: 'an', explain: 'thing 是单数可数名词，缺冠词，应为 not an easy thing。' },
      { no: 10, type: '改', from: 'much bravely', to: 'much braver', explain: 'than 前要用比较级，且 feel 后接形容词 braver，副词 bravely 不能作表语。' },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'ef6',
    title: '农场劳动的一天',
    exam: '中考',
    mins: 7,
    lines: [
      { no: 1, text: 'Dear Chris, Last Friday our class goes to a farm near the city, and we got there early by bus.' },
      { no: 2, text: 'Our teacher divided us into four groups, and each group was responsible for a piece of land in the farm.' },
      { no: 3, text: 'Uncle Wang, one of the farmers there, showed us how to plant tomatos, beans and potatoes.' },
      { no: 4, text: 'He gave the smallest tools to we students and laughed at our funny faces.' },
      { no: 5, text: 'It was best day of my life, and I took many photos on the long hill behind the house.' },
      { no: 6, text: 'At noon we sat under a big tree and enjoyed to eat the apples Uncle Wang gave us.' },
      { no: 7, text: 'The farmers gave us a basket of apples because we worked hard, but we were very happy.' },
      { no: 8, text: 'On the way back, Uncle Wang talked us about the food on our table and how much water rice needs.' },
      { no: 9, text: 'In my opinion, farm work is very much harder than sitting in a classroom all day.' },
      { no: 10, text: 'Every one of us were happy that day, and I hope you can come with me next term.' },
    ],
    fixes: [
      { no: 1, type: '改', from: 'class goes', to: 'class went', explain: 'Last Friday 是明确的过去时间，谓语用一般过去时。' },
      { no: 2, type: '改', from: 'in the farm', to: 'on the farm', explain: '农场、土地前用介词 on，on the farm 是固定搭配。' },
      { no: 3, type: '改', from: 'tomatos', to: 'tomatoes', explain: '以 o 结尾有生命的名词复数加 -es，tomato 的复数是 tomatoes。' },
      { no: 4, type: '改', from: 'to we', to: 'to us', explain: '介词 to 后接宾格 us，we 是主格。' },
      { no: 5, type: '增', from: 'was', to: 'the', explain: '最高级 best day 前缺定冠词 the，应为 it was the best day。' },
      { no: 6, type: '改', from: 'enjoyed to eat', to: 'enjoyed eating', explain: 'enjoy 后接动名词作宾语，不接不定式。' },
      { no: 7, type: '改', from: 'but', to: 'so', explain: '前后是因果关系“劳动辛苦，所以收到苹果很高兴”，用 so。' },
      { no: 8, type: '增', from: 'talked', to: 'to', explain: 'talk to sb about sth 缺介词 to，应为 talked to us。' },
      { no: 9, type: '删', from: 'very', to: '删去 very', explain: '比较级 harder 由 much 修饰，very 多余且不能修饰比较级。' },
      { no: 10, type: '改', from: 'us were', to: 'us was', explain: '主语 every one 是单数，谓语用 was。' },
    ],
  },
